{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310808,"nonce":"DBwNlB5VODKskK4PAM4Em2gIMuA=","title":"rayzor.* near-native audit (2026-06-17) — wasm value types don't inline (L1), atomics unimplemented (L2), Ptr\u003cT\u003e stride bug (L3), ...","message":"13-agent codegen-verified audit of the rayzor.* namespace for Rust/C++ parity (workflow wf_0e9d523b). Full report: task wk0zys2pm output. THREE LOWERING TIERS, parity only on Tier A:\n\n- **Tier A — truly zero-cost, BOTH backends: only SIMD4f OPERATORS** (`+ - * /`, `v[const]`). Short-circuit at the call site to `VectorBinOp`/`VectorExtract` (hir_to_mir.rs:19092-19124, 8974-9006) → `f32x4.*`/NEON inline, `a*b+c`→`F32x4RelaxedMadd` (wasm_backend.rs:2595). Zero SIMD4f host imports on wasm. THE anchor/model.\n- **Tier B — stack value (i64), inline IR body, but the CALL is never inlined on wasm/JIT: Ptr/Ref/Box/Usize + SIMD4f NAMED methods.** `convert_type` forces these → IrType::I64 (hir_to_mir.rs:21610); bodies are pure inline (`Ptr_deref`=1 load systems.rs:291). Zero-cost ONLY on AOT-native, because native re-runs PassManager on the MERGED module (aot_compiler.rs:215,761) but the wasm/Cranelift-JIT path feeds the merged module straight to codegen with NO re-opt → wrappers stay CallDirect. This is THE wasm-native gap.\n- **Tier C — FFI-over-heap-handle: Tensor/QTensor/Vec/Bytes/Arc/Mutex/Map/String.** Each method → `builder.call(rayzor_*/haxe_*)` extern = guest→host crossing on wasm. Fine for heavy kernels (matmul amortizes); pure tax for cheap metadata/elementwise.\n\nSMART-PTR/ATOMIC GAP (user-flagged, real + stronger than \"under-leveraged\"): **atomics ENTIRELY unimplemented** — `haxe.atomic.AtomicInt/Bool/Object` have NO @:native/mapping/IR (0 hits compiler/src), IR `Instruction` enum has Vector* but ZERO atomic variants. A Haxe program cannot do one atomic load/store/CAS. **Arc/Mutex are FFI-over-handle AND FAKE on wasm**: `rayzor_arc_init/clone/get` identity no-ops, `strong_count` hardcoded 1, Mutex = single-thread host HashMap, box_free no-op (wasm_runner.rs:3779-3827). `@:shared`+`@:derive(Clone)` atomic-refcount is Tensor/QTensor-ONLY. nue's Haxe is 100% single-threaded (0 rayzor.concurrent/haxe.atomic across 52 files); all parallelism is in the Rust kernels.\n\nVERIFIED BUG **L3**: `Ptr_offset` hardcodes `n*8` (systems.rs:317, comment \"element size is i64=8\") + wasm PtrAdd GEP scales U8/I8=1 else 8 (wasm_backend.rs:2964) → **Ptr\u003cFloat\u003e/Ptr\u003ci32\u003e (4-byte) stride by 8 = reads wrong memory.** Latent (nue may not use Ptr\u003cf32\u003e yet) but GATES L5.\n\nRANKED LEVERS (to close the wasm orchestration gap, ~42% of decode step):\n- **L3 — DONE (commit 656b599, 2026-06-17).** Fixed via size-typed wrapper variants (Ptr_offset_{1,4}/Ptr_deref_{1,4,4f}/Ptr_write_{1,4,4f} in systems.rs), call-site redirect by pointee type in hir_to_mir.rs (~9906), signatures in runtime_mapping.rs. KEY: wrapper ptr param MUST stay IrType::I64 (not Ptr\u003celem\u003e) or Cranelift is_struct_field sign-extends narrow stores to 8B. Did NOT touch the frozen GEP/PtrAdd arms (HaxeArray 8B stride preserved). Byte-identical-inert (no narrow-pointee consumer yet) → enables L5. Verified Paris + 132/0 haxe (test_exception crash is pre-existing+intermittent, confirmed via stash).\n- **L1 — DONE (commit 1f3d800).** Run one InliningPass on the merged module in src/compile_helpers.rs:153, gated on the \"wasm\" define (native AOT untouched — it re-runs its own PassManager). Cost model max_inline_size=50 inlines the 1-3 instr leaves; no Always stamps needed. NEUTRAL on nue decode today (28.5 vs ~30ms, within noise) — it's the enabler for L5, not a standalone win.\n- **L5 — REASSESSED, payoff UNCERTAIN/likely SMALL on the in-guest path.** The audit framed L5 as \"biggest wasm-decode win\" assuming Tensor ops are HOST FFI (Tier C). But nue decode runs IN-GUEST: rmsnorm/rope/softmax/flash/elementwise are runtime-wasm/kernels.rs (in-guest calls, already SIMD128), NOT host crossings. So L5's benefit on the actual path is alloc-reduction (allocs are only 0.5-2.3% of decode per [[perf_q4km_sdot_4way_unroll]]) + call overhead + fusion, NOT host-crossing removal → probably a few %, not 3×. MEASURE the matmul-vs-attention-vs-elementwise split before committing to the big L5 change. Real remaining ~3× gap (wasm 28ms vs native 10.5ms) is the matmul/attention KERNEL codegen (Cranelift JIT ~1.4× native) + single-threaded in-guest flash, not the orchestration.\n- **L5 (big, biggest raw wasm-decode win): lower Tensor elementwise (rmsNorm/silu/mul/add/RoPE) to inline SIMD4f+Ptr loops** instead of tensor_* FFI + fresh result tensor. Removes a host crossing + a heap alloc per op. Needs L1+L3.\n- **L2+L8 (big, the flagged gap): real atomic IR family + rayzor.Atomic\u003cT\u003e + real wasm Arc/Mutex** (shared-mem atomic refcount, memory.atomic.wait/notify). Unlocks Haxe-level parallelism: band the elementwise orchestration, Arc the KV cache/weights zero-copy, lock-free worker counters.\n- minor: L6 clone/free elision, L7 nue StringMap→Int-id Vec, L10 niche-pack Option/Result (boxes today), L11 closures do TWO mallocs (env not stack-allocated despite escape_analysis.rs existing).\n\nALSO settled 2026-06-17: **RAYZOR_WORKERS / RAYZOR_NO_PARK do NOT affect in-guest wasm decode** (in-guest = runtime-wasm/kernels.rs self-contained; worker_pool::global() is runtime/src native-only). Measured flat p50 across WORKERS 6/8/10 + clean-vs-NO_PARK alternating = overlapping noise. NO_PARK can only HURT in-guest (spinning native threads contend with the guest pool). Fast wasm config = just default (or RAYZOR_WASM_NO_HOST_MATMUL=1); drop WORKERS/NO_PARK. See [[perf_wasm_host_parallel_matmul]].\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `perf_rayzor_namespace_near_native` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}